OL,3,GNEWSA'My wife would still be alive if  
OL,4,ANHS Grampian had followed medical      
OL,5,Aguidelines'                            
OL,7,FThe husband of an Aberdeenshire woman  
OL,8,Fwho died from cancer says she would    
OL,9,Fstill be alive if NHS Grampian had     
OL,10,Ffollowed medical guidelines.           
OL,12,FJohn Fotheringham, whose wife Helen    
OL,13,Fdied aged 64 in September 2022, has    
OL,14,Faccused the crisis-ridden health board 
OL,15,Fof "lies, obstruction and suppression  
OL,16,Fof evidence".                          
OL,18,FA review into Helen's death from       
OL,19,Foesophageal cancer found opportunities 
OL,20,Fto save her life were missed - and     
OL,21,Fwarned similar failings may have       
OL,22,Faffected other patients.               
OL,23,APub: 26-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
